{"abstract":"Writing and genre conventions are extant to any scientific community, and CHI is no different. In this paper, we present the early phases of an AI tool called KITSUNE, which takes text and adapts it toward the writing conventions of a CHI paper. We describe the development of the tool with the intent to promote discussion around how writing conventions are upheld and unquestioned by the CHI community, and how this translates to the work produced. In addition, we bring up questions surrounding how the introduction of LLMs into academic writing will fundamentally change how conventions will be upheld now and in the future.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Robinson, Raquel","Alvarez, Alberto","Mekler, Elisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747247"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University"],"keyword":["AI","Artificial intelligence","CHI","LLMs","writing conventions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to write a chi paper asking for a friend","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105577670/3613905.3644051.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747247","identifier":[{"id":"85194168851","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8cbb36c9-52bf-4247-b237-85b5a0e31aa9"],"keyword":["AI","CHI","LLMs","artificial intelligence","writing conventions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A57D600E7080D8DBC56813599FADDDF2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/105577670/3613905.3644051.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human-Centered Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raquel","key":"robinsonpau","last":"Robinson","locid":"cb1b6c5f-6206-4a35-b8aa-6a750f9c89a1","name":"Robinson, Raquel","orcid":"0000-0003-4933-7168","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alberto","key":"alvarezpau","last":"Alvarez","name":"Alvarez, Alberto","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"meklerpau","last":"Mekler","locid":"cf6cfa0b-e3ac-4164-8de2-b956d8e23825","name":"Mekler, Elisa","orcid":"0000-0003-0076-6703","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3613905.3644051","isbn":["9798400703317"],"status":"p","title":"CHI EA '24: Extended Abstracts of the 2024 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194168851"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8cbb36c9-52bf-4247-b237-85b5a0e31aa9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How to write a CHI paper (asking for a friend)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747247","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"STEM education is an important component of broadening participation in computational fields, and robotics-inspired kits are a common avenue for teaching youth computational concepts. In this pictorial, we contrast widely used kits (i.e., Lego Mindstorms, Sphero, and DASH) with a kit we created in the form of a module embedded in a summer camp, that takes an alternative approach. Most existing kits are designed with clear-cut, narrowly defined end goals for learners to accomplish. The lessons typically do not include teaching design concepts, and do not offer opportunities for crafting, personalization, and storytelling. We offer a more flexible and creative kit design; integrating concepts such as design thinking, iterative design, and collaboration. We illustrate our design process used to craft the kit/module, along with artifacts collected from its use, and discuss how this approach might help support a broader range of groups—particularly those that are underrepresented in STEM.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fey, James","Robinson, Raquel","Ovali, Selin","Laffan, Nate","Weatherwax, Kevin","Dagan, Ella","Isbister, Katherine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730205"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California"],"keyword":["Computational Learning","Design thinking","Robotics Kits","STEM education","Underrepresented Groups in STEM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"now that s what i call a robot ics education kit","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3623509.3633401","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730205","identifier":[{"id":"85185222506","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f88d1567-467b-4fb4-a1a0-f6a2aab49229"],"keyword":["Computational Learning","Design Thinking","Robotics Kits","STEM Education","Underrepresented Groups in STEM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F4B34DB815E011D31CF8CF97A23FB3A1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102807159/tei24-53_3_.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3623509.3633401","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Human-Centered Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"feypau","last":"Fey","name":"Fey, James","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Raquel","key":"robinsonpau","last":"Robinson","locid":"cb1b6c5f-6206-4a35-b8aa-6a750f9c89a1","name":"Robinson, Raquel","orcid":"0000-0003-4933-7168","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Selin","key":"ovalipau","last":"Ovali","name":"Ovali, Selin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nate","key":"laffanpau","last":"Laffan","name":"Laffan, Nate","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kevin","key":"weatherwaxpau","last":"Weatherwax","name":"Weatherwax, Kevin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ella","key":"daganpau","last":"Dagan","name":"Dagan, Ella","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katherine","key":"isbisterpau","last":"Isbister","name":"Isbister, Katherine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3623509.3633401","isbn":["9798400704024"],"pages":"1-14","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Tangible, Embedded, and Embodied Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f88d1567-467b-4fb4-a1a0-f6a2aab49229"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Now That's What I Call a Robot(ics Education Kit)!","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730205","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Literature reviews (or \"lit reviews\" for short) have become a popular way of knowing in HCI, yet there has been little reflection as to what we want from these reviews and how they can benefit the HCI design research community. Pushes toward more rigor and adopting standards within lit reviews often seem inappropriate and at odds with ways of knowing within the design research community. In this paper, we present critiques and associated risks of these viewpoints, and reflections towards a more thoughtful engagement with literature reviews in HCI design research. We open a discussion of how literature reviews currently inform research, and how we think they could better do so in the future","author_count":2,"contributors":["Robinson, Raquel","Mekler, Elisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776377"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Literature review","Research synthesis","Rigor","Systematic review","Transparency","Ways of knowing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reflections towards more thoughtful engagement with literature reviews in hci","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3686169.3686183","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funded by the European Union (MSCA-PF, RAGE, 101154545; ERC, THEORYCRAFT, 101043198)."],"id":"S01-000.00-776377","identifier":[{"id":"85215514207","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1bdc44ec-a22a-42bd-ab9a-5d6eedf3b783"],"keyword":["literature review","research synthesis","rigor","systematic review","transparency","ways of knowing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AA7B4EDEB58C081676BACC1A69C0EBD4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3686169.3686183","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raquel","key":"robinsonpau","last":"Robinson","locid":"cb1b6c5f-6206-4a35-b8aa-6a750f9c89a1","name":"Robinson, Raquel","orcid":"0000-0003-4933-7168","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"meklerpau","last":"Mekler","locid":"cf6cfa0b-e3ac-4164-8de2-b956d8e23825","name":"Mekler, Elisa","orcid":"0000-0003-0076-6703","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3686169.3686183","status":"p","title":"HttF '24: Proceedings of the Halfway to the Future Symposium"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85215514207"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1bdc44ec-a22a-42bd-ab9a-5d6eedf3b783"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reflections Towards More Thoughtful Engagement with Literature Reviews in HCI","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776377","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In the first-ever Undiagnosed Hackathon, nearly 100 experts from 28 countries combined advanced phenotyping and genomic techniques for 48 hours, ultimately providing diagnoses to 40% of the previously undiagnosed families. This inspiring model demonstrates the power of multidisciplinary collaboration and patient partnership in precision diagnostics.","author_count":104,"contributors":["Delgado-Vega, Angelica Maria","Cederroth, Helene","Taylan, Fulya","Ekholm, Katja","Ek, Marlene","Thonberg, Håkan","Jemt, Anders","Nilsson, Daniel","Eisfeldt, Jesper","Bilgrav Saether, Kristine","Höijer, Ida","Akgun-Dogan, Ozlem","Asano, Yui","Barakat, Tahsin Stefan","Batkovskyte, Dominyka","Baynam, Gareth","Bodamer, Olaf","Chetruengchai, Wanna","Corcoran, Pádraic","Couse, Madeline","Danis, Daniel","Demidov, German","Dohi, Eisuke","Erhardsson, Mattias","Fernandez-Luna, Luis","Fujiwara, Toyofumi","Garg, Neha","Giugliani, Roberto","Gonzaga-Jauregui, Claudia","Grigelioniene, Giedre","Groza, Tudor","Gunnarsson, Cecilia","Hammarsjö, Anna","Hammond, Charles Kumi","Hatirnaz Ng, Özden","Hesketh, Sirisha","Hettiarachchi, Dineshani","Johansson Soller, Maria","Kirmani, Umn Ahmed","Kjellberg, Martin","Kvarnung, Malin","Kvlividze, Oleg","Lagerstedt-Robinson, Kristina","Lasko, Paul","Lassmann, Timo","Lau, Lynette Y.S.","Laurie, Steven","Lim, Weng Khong","Liu, Zhandong","Lysenkova Wiklander, Mariya","Makay, Prince","Maiga, Alassane Baneye","Maya-González, Carolina","Meyn, M. Stephen","Neethiraj, Ramprasad","Nigro, Vincenzo","Nordgren, Felix","Nordlund, Jessica","Orrsjö, Sara","Ottosson, Jesper","Ozbek, Ugur","Özdemir, Özkan","Partin, Clyde","Pearce, David A.","Peck, Raquel","Pedersen, Annie","Pettersson, Maria","Pongpanich, Monnat","Posada de la Paz, Manuel","Ramani, Arun","Romero, Juan Andres","Romero, Vanessa I.","Rosenquist, Richard","Saw, Aung Min","Spencer, Matthew","Stattin, Eva Lena","Srichomthong, Chalurmpon","Tapia-Paez, Isabel","Taruscio, Domenica","Taylor, Julie P.","Tkemaladz